                  "heading": "Grounds and Outdoor Spaces"
                },
                "ordered": false,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cendara Arboretum (20 acres): Managed collection of native and exotic plants, walking trails, and an outdoor classroom amphitheater.",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "East Lake: Man-made, 3-acre lake with surrounding picnic and study areas.",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Reflection Garden: Dedicated quiet zone adjacent to Samuelson Library, used for meditation and outdoor study.",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bike & Pedestrian Paths: Five miles of interconnected, ADA-accessible trails linking all campus sectors.",
                    "depth": 0
                  }
